#: 9576a6b98bca43a2a645ef251af31b1a
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:14
#: 9f607f474ac74615afe47b2532b2de20
msgid ""
"A **Count-Min Sketch** (CMS) estimates the frequency of elements in a "
"data stream using a compact :math:`d \\times w` counter matrix. Like the "
"Bloom Filter, it may **overestimate** but never underestimates a true "
"frequency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:19
#: 0e3002cdd5a34224938a0159526efd65
msgid "Mathematical Foundations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:22
#: 5741630858fe43a6b25032e9134a159d
msgid "Counter Matrix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:24
#: 51d99059972c42dda58e1fb48da21333
msgid ""
"A CMS is a matrix :math:`C[d][w]` of non-negative integer counters, "
"initialised to 0, with :math:`d` hash functions :math:`h_1, \\ldots, h_d "
": U \\to [0, w)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:28
#: 4e4f0312148547a5b52b1626778cc9f2
msgid "**Add** element :math:`x`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:30
#: e4e99f93759b480d840f37481a789099
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\forall i \\in [1, d] : C[i][h_i(x)] \\mathrel{+}= 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:34
#: b86644a3892b48b19c94b1d603c5d7bf
msgid "**Estimate** frequency of :math:`x`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:36
#: 9b1e0526f88f48f88b1ea8c0322d517d
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\hat{f}(x) = \\min_{i=1}^{d} C[i][h_i(x)]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:41
#: 6202f46f66524c808291c25e6784194b
msgid "Probabilistic Guarantee"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:43
#: dfba627d5afe4221910f024b074b129f
msgid ""
"Let :math:`N` be the total number of elements added. With probability "
":math:`\\geq 1 - \\delta`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:46
#: 48470c65a9f640c6b2ef8b4998829683
#, python-brace-format
msgid "f(x) \\leq \\hat{f}(x) \\leq f(x) + \\varepsilon \\cdot N"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:50
#: bf999290f7ad4fd8af471253b49ff9a0
msgid "Optimal dimensions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:52
#: 78b5bb7334274773942e5254cdea62e7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"w = \\left\\lceil \\frac{e}{\\varepsilon} \\right\\rceil\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"d = \\left\\lceil \\ln\\frac{1}{\\delta} \\right\\rceil"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:58
#: 2395ed36c8cb4e3a9dbbdf76e0db6ea2
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**No false negatives**: :math:`\\hat{f}(x) \\geq f(x)` always holds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:61
#: f47d1c17e3314166ad5dd21bb1c6c33e
msgid "Double Hashing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:63
#: 7c2b8d813d77401299ed22840703b41d
msgid ""
"As with the Bloom Filter, the CMS uses double hashing to avoid computing "
":math:`d` fully independent hash functions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/advanced_structures/count_min_sketch.rst:66
#: 8992429eaff14ec6bb7d92874b80b43a
msgid "h_i(x) = (h_1(x) + i \\cdot h_2(x)) \\bmod w"
msgstr ""

